diff --git a/docs/adr/0011-consumer-route-state.md b/docs/adr/0011-consumer-route-state.md
index a9b05a1..6541306 100644
--- a/docs/adr/0011-consumer-route-state.md
+++ b/docs/adr/0011-consumer-route-state.md
@@ -61,3 +61,15 @@ Safe legacy startup now consumes the codec for time/focus/layers/scale/view and
 P4.2 applies parsed frame settings and is reviewed accepted. P4.3 routes/metadata/lifetime are reviewed accepted and committed as `1f778e3`. P4.4 synchronization/sharing is reviewed accepted. No providers, physical models, assets or scientific tolerances change. P4.2's exact orbit sampling endpoint correction preserves strict provider validity without changing those bounds or model output.
 
 Retry-4 passes both hardware timing cases and all other cases except that history precondition: it counts Next's internal same-URL replacement as another command. The installed app-router HistoryUpdater and native history patch explain the two calls. The corrected test records the incoming __NA marker without modifying history data, requires one external and one internal replacement of the same href, then requires zero further writes through playback/gestures. A focused immutable-production verification passes sharing and exact paused reload too. Runtime and thresholds remain unchanged; full exact-source validation is pending.
+
+P4.5 is reviewed accepted and committed locally as b9e47bb: all 44 production cases pass, warm lookup max 0.6099 ms and verified Radeon 780M response maxima 58.9 ms desktop / 27.9 ms phone viewport. Earlier software timing failures remain preserved; final shell long-task gates remain P4.9.
+
+P4.6 extracts ObjectCard/ObjectMetrics/ProvenanceDetails/MobileObjectSheet. Catalog kinds and explicit known giant/rocky IDs replace blanket terrestrial labels. Physical Sun/Earth distances and SSB speed use the public getMetrics getter; diameter/period use actual catalog values. Missing/nonfinite fields show Unavailable; small positive AU values retain scientific notation rather than rounding to zero. Miles use 1.609344 km and AU 149597870.7 km; speed uses mi/s for mile preference and km/s for AU.
+
+A small objectSnapshot adapter keeps astronomy UTC conversion inside the engine bridge, as required by package boundaries. The card samples public getters from the existing <=4 Hz perf bridge; no frame callback or new clock/render subscription is added. Distance preference moves into the current UI store for card/history coherence; versioned persistence remains P4.7.
+
+Provenance shows actual catalog provider/source URL, method, certainty, uncertainty note and simulation UTC. JPL residual corrections are identified only for the currently corrected astronomy bodies/Callisto; other Galilean moons retain analytic wording. Source timestamp, ingestion date and model epoch are shown only when supplied; simulation time is explicitly separate. No invented timestamps, telemetry or new provider/data source.
+
+One card DOM serves desktop and mobile. Keyboard reachable Peek/Half/Full controls retain focus; content scrolls internally and card pointer/touch/wheel/keyboard events stop at its boundary. Header/close and snap controls stay outside scrolling content. Short-height portrait/landscape layout keeps the card above the timeline and exposes full content by scrolling. Disclosure/follow/refocus/show-hide layer/share use public commands and the existing semantic route/share path. Closing returns focus to Find a world. Source values are independent of True/Explore display scale.
+
+P4.6 short verify passes 372 tests plus two existing expected rejections / 42 files, including 29 formatter/provenance tests. Initial verification caught an astronomy import in UI; moving UTC conversion to the bridge fixes it without weakening boundaries. Browser discovery is 53 cases in ten files: nine new card/mobile cases and all 44 prior checks. Production/budget/science/browser review is pending before P4.6 acceptance.
